r maintenance shop to his skills and hard work paying off, which he finds incredible.\n  - car maintenance shop: Dave's car maintenance shop lost a deal they pursued for months to a competing shop, making Dave feel bummed out despite his hard work.\n  - Dave: Dave attended a car workshop in San Francisco to learn car restoration techniques. He also had a card night with friends last Friday and discussed his ongoing car restoration project with Calvin.\n  - car mod workshop: Dave attended a car mod workshop in San Francisco to learn about car restoration techniques and pursue his passion for auto engineering and custom car building.\n  - Dave: Dave's band had a fun rehearsal session last night. Last weekend, Dave attended a rock concert in Boston. Dave is also praised by Calvin for fixing cars.\n  - dad: Dave's dad took him to his first car show when he was 10, which sparked his interest in cars. Dave later became an automotive engineer.\n  - automotive engineer: Dave is an automotive engineer whose interest started at age 10 after attending a car show with his dad. He finds building powerful cars from small parts cool.\n  - Dave: Dave recently returned from San Francisco with insights on car modification, finding satisfaction in fixing and improving old cars to help others.\n  - local garage: Dave is teaming up with a local garage for a new venture, which Calvin congratulated him on opening.\n  - car stuff: Dave is tied up with car stuff, recently returned from San Francisco with knowledge on car modification. He listens to vinyl while working on cars to relax and stay productive.\n  - garage: Dave's garage is a little dirty but everything is in place; it's where he tinkers with cars, an activity he finds calming. Calvin looks forward to seeing it.\n  - Dave: Dave previously enjoyed a card night and is restoring a car for his auto engineering goal. He chatted with Calvin about Calvin's amazing performance on a big stage.\n  - Dave: Dave is restoring a Ford Mustang f