". Previously, John volunteered programming skills for a charitable foundation and got his dream job.\n  - John: John volunteered programming skills for a social cause, creating software to streamline operations for a charitable foundation, which he found rewarding.\n  - work: James is learning new programming stuff and is looking for ideas to incorporate into his work. John previously started a new startup involving portable smokers.\n  - John: John held a Fortnite gaming tournament with friends, raising money for a children's hospital.\n  - John: John organized an online competition with programmer friends and congratulated James on releasing his game.\n  - John: John organized an online competition with programmer friends last week and congratulated James on releasing his first game.\n  - John: John expressed empathy to James about losing power during a game and later asked James about his mother's friend possibly still being in the army.\n  - John: John is working on a cool coding project with his siblings, which is a game to help them learn. He is also working on his first professional website for a small business.\n  - John: John organized an online programming competition and expressed gratitude for James' support. He was told about James losing power during a game and asked about a seminar he attended.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer to create a unique online board game and ended a conversation with James about it. Previously, he won a chess tournament and organized charity gaming tournaments.\n  - John: John is communicating with James, expressing sympathy about James losing power mid-game and asking if it affected his progress.\n  - John: John is working on his first professional website project for a local small business and is currently playing AC Valhalla.\n  - John: John is loving sharing his coding journey and tracking everything. He also bought many new books, almost completely filling his bookcase.\n  - John: John plays drums, won