ks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - outdoors: Audrey misses taking her dogs for walks in nature, calling those moments with her pets in the outdoors chill and happy.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - my little family: Audrey described 'my little family' as people who always make her smile, give love and companionship. She also mentioned getting more drawings added to her tattoo of her four dogs.\n  - bond: Audrey's bond with her pup felt stronger after chasing and calming her down following a broken leash incident at the park.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n  - pooches: Pooches moved to a new place with a bigger backyard for running and exploring. Audrey calmed her pooch, Precious, by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly; patience and practice help establish bonds with pooches.\n  - dog: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon for grooming. Andrew adopted another dog recently, managing with two dogs currently, and asked Audrey for multi-dog owner tips.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - her pups: One of Audrey's pups pulled so hard on the leash last Friday at the park that it busted; she chased and caught the pup. Audrey calmed her by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - winter: Audrey's dogs hate snow, and they were confused when taken to a snowy park last winter, preferring sunny days.\n  - Audrey (assistant): Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist last Wednesday for her dogs who were acting abnormally and received tips to help with their problems.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - dog-friendly place: Audrey made goodies to thank neighbors for their pup-friendly homes. Previously, Audrey encouraged Andrew to find a great dog-friendly place to live.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - dog owners: Audrey meets with a dog owners group once a week for tips and playdates. She considered a positive reinforcement training class workshop advertised at her pet store.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2063,"context_chars":7865,"retrieva